    "title": "Reflecting on the Project",
    "long_instructions": "#### As students work on their cybersecurity projects, balancing technical structure with creative exploration is key — thoughtful scaffolds, guided analysis of security trade-offs, and opportunities for peer critique will help them transform their ideas into well-reasoned, user-focused solutions.\r\n\r\n## Discussion Questions: \r\n#### 1️⃣ How will I help students move beyond surface-level issues to identify deeper security problems in a system?\r\n\r\n#### 2️⃣ What strategies can I use to support students in balancing creativity (e.g., personified defense mechanisms) with technical accuracy?\r\n\r\n#### 3️⃣ How will I guide students to explain trade-offs in their solutions rather than focusing only on the “best” fix?\r\n\r\n#### *These questions are just starting points for reflection — there is no need to answer all of them. Focus on the ones that resonate most with your teaching experience and goals.*\r\n",
